    "## 11. Inventory the actual CSV files\n",
    "\n",
    "This step records what is genuinely present. It does not assume the dataset contains all common city- and station-level tables.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each CSV, the inventory includes:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Filename (not its full directory path).\n",
    "- File size.\n",
    "- Parsed record count.\n",
    "- Column names.\n",
    "- Date coverage when a recognizable date column exists.\n",
    "- SHA-256 checksum for provenance and future integrity checks.\n",
    "\n",
    "CSV record counting uses Python's CSV reader, which counts logical records rather than simply counting newline characters. Date coverage is scanned in chunks to avoid loading all files into memory."
   ]
  },
