   "source": [
    "# AQI-Cast India — Notebook 01: Dataset Acquisition\n",
    "\n",
    "**Notebook:** `01_dataset_acquisition.ipynb`  \n",
    "**Phase:** Project Foundation  \n",
    "**Primary output:** `artifacts/dataset_manifest.json`  \n",
    "**Raw-data area:** `data/raw/`\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook acquires or imports the historical **Air Quality Data in India** collection, inventories the files actually available, inspects the city-level daily dataset, and records a reproducible dataset manifest.\n",
    "\n",
    "The collection is published on Kaggle by Rohan Rao and is described by the Transport Data Commons metadata record as compiled from data provided by India's Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB). Its reference period is **1 January 2015 to 31 December 2020**. It is historical data, not a source of current 2026 observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Kaggle collection may contain multiple CSV tables (for example, city-level daily/hourly and station-level daily/hourly data). This notebook does not assume every file is present. It inventories the actual download and uses `city_day.csv` by default because AQI-Cast India's initial target is **city-level daily AQI**.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Establish the same project paths and conventions used in Notebook 00.\n",
    "2. Support KaggleHub acquisition and local/manual dataset import.\n",
    "3. Avoid printing absolute or unnecessary relative filesystem paths.\n",
    "4. Inventory available CSV files, file sizes, row counts, schemas, date ranges, and SHA-256 checksums.\n",
    "5. Load and inspect the primary city-level daily file without silently changing or cleaning its values.\n",
    "6. Validate the minimum fields needed by the forecasting pipeline: `City`, `Date`, and `AQI`.\n",
    "7. Save a traceable dataset manifest in `artifacts/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Data source and provenance\n",
    "\n",
    "| Item | Source information |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Dataset | Air Quality Data in India (2015–2020) |\n",
    "| Kaggle handle | `rohanrao/air-quality-data-in-india` |\n",
    "| Compiler | Rohan Rao, as stated in the metadata record |\n",
    "| Upstream data provider | Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB), India |\n",
    "| Reference period | 2015-01-01 to 2020-12-31 |\n",
    "| Metadata-listed license | CC0 1.0 on the Transport Data Commons record; re-check the Kaggle listing when acquiring data |\n",
    "| Main forecasting file | `city_day.csv` |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Source links**\n",
    "\n",
    "- [Kaggle dataset page](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rohanrao/air-quality-data-in-india)\n",
    "- [Transport Data Commons dataset metadata](https://portal.transport-data.org/@tumi/urban-air-pollution-india-2015-2020)\n",
    "- [KaggleHub documentation](https://github.com/Kaggle/kagglehub)\n",
    "\n",
    "KaggleHub documents `dataset_download()` for downloading dataset files and supports a custom output directory in current releases. Authentication can be required for datasets that require user consent or for private resources. The notebook never prints or stores API tokens.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Technical approach\n",
    "\n",
    "The acquisition mode can be selected as:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `auto`: use a local `city_day.csv` already under the raw-data area; otherwise attempt KaggleHub if it is installed.\n",
    "- `local`: use a manually downloaded/extracted dataset folder.\n",
    "- `kagglehub`: explicitly download the Kaggle dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "The raw source files remain in `data/raw/`. The generated manifest is saved in `artifacts/`. No chart is required in this acquisition notebook, so no image is generated.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Dependencies and execution order\n",
    "\n",
    "Run `00_environment_setup.ipynb` first. Then run every cell in this notebook from top to bottom.\n",
    "\n",
    "Required for inspection: Python 3.10+, Pandas, and NumPy. KaggleHub is optional when the data has already been downloaded manually.\n",
    "\n",
    "If KaggleHub is not installed, install it in the active notebook environment with `%pip install -U kagglehub`, then restart the kernel if required. Alternatively, download the dataset from Kaggle in a browser and extract its CSV files into the project's `data/raw/` area.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Credentials:** Do not paste API tokens into notebook cells or commit credential files. Follow KaggleHub's official authentication instructions using an approved local credential mechanism if authentication is required."
   ]
