    "## 17. Outputs and handoff to Notebook 02\n",
    "\n",
    "### Generated output\n",
    "\n",
    "| Output | Location | Purpose |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `dataset_manifest.json` | `artifacts/` | Provenance, file inventory, checksums, schema, coverage, and validation summary |\n",
    "| Original source CSV files | `data/raw/` | Immutable input data for downstream processing |\n",
    "\n",
    "No charts are generated in this notebook. Any future charts must be saved under `images/`, and every generated data/model/report file must be saved under `artifacts/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dependency for the next notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "`02_data_validation.ipynb` should read the primary city-level daily source and the manifest generated here. It must independently validate missingness, duplicate city-date records, date continuity, numeric ranges, and city-level data availability before any cleaning decisions are made.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Important cautions\n",
    "\n",
    "- Do not interpret the source reference period as current air-quality coverage.\n",
    "- Do not treat rows as equally spaced or complete until date continuity is checked per city.\n",
    "- Do not infer a pollution value when AQI or pollutant measurements are missing.\n",
    "- Do not merge station-level and city-level tables without a documented key and aggregation strategy.\n",
    "- Preserve the original raw data; data cleaning belongs in the next phase.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 18. Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "- Kaggle download access can depend on network conditions, Kaggle consent requirements, or authentication settings.\n",
    "- The dataset's actual files and columns can change between revisions; the notebook records the version encountered at runtime but does not assume a fixed bundle.\n",
    "- CSV row counting and checksum calculation read the source files; very large future dataset releases may take additional time.\n",
    "- A valid primary schema is only an acquisition gate. It is not evidence that the data is clean or suitable for a reliable forecast.\n",
    "- The initial dataset cannot support a claim of live AQI forecasting for 2026.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 19. Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "The acquisition stage is complete when the primary city-level daily table is available, the minimum `City` / `Date` / `AQI` schema passes, and `dataset_manifest.json` has been generated. Continue to Notebook 02 only after reviewing any action-required checks and confirming that the measured coverage makes sense for the downloaded version."
